 is **ignoring the death relationship rules** in the CROSS_GROUP_SYSTEM prompt (lines 105-115) and recommending a merge despite clear evidence they are separate entities who interact in a death scene.\n\n**Why the death detection isn't working:**\n1. The `_entities_in_death_relationship()` function (lines 1963-2042) checks if BOTH entity names appear together in a death context\n2. The function looks for patterns like \"fell prostrate in death\" (line 1982)\n3. It searches for both \"mummer\" and \"prospero\" (or parts of \"Prince Prospero\") in the same context\n4. **BUT**: The LLM is being asked FIRST (line 2228), and if it says \"merge\", the code-based check happens AFTER (lines 2258-2266)\n5. **The problem**: The LLM is returning a merge recommendation, then the death check runs but may not be finding both names in the SAME context snippet due to how contexts are chunked\n\n**Confidence:** HIGH - I've traced the exact code path and identified that the LLM is recommending the merge despite the prompt rules.\n\nNow let me document this and move to implementing a fix:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3627,"cache_read_input_tokens":80731,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3627,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"510b9767-e567-40b5-bc06-3d57a25e9010","uuid":"9e6af5fd-be56-46ae-ac78-9dc9c280a57d"}
